body:
Change array/slice patterns in the following ways:
- Make them only match on arrays (`[T, ..n]` and `[T]`), not slices (#478);
- Make subslice matching yield a value of type `[T, ..n]` or `[T]`, not `&[T]` or `&mut [T]`;
- Allow multiple mutable references to be made to different parts of the same array or slice in array patterns (resolving rust-lang/rust#8636).

[Rendered](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/0495-array-pattern-changes.md)

Executive summary:

``` rust
impl<T: Int + !Float> Average for T { ... }
impl<T: Float + !Int> Average for T { ... }
impl<T: Int + Float> Average for T { ... }
```

[Rendered](https://github.com/kennytm/rfcs/blob/neg-bounds/text/0000-negative-bounds.md)

cc #442, #290, rust-lang/rust#19032.
